00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
because when you got a corset on my  waist was about 20 inches and you  absolutely can't breathe  sailing the high seas and getting into  swashbuckling pirate fights  may seem like a good time but  transforming yourself into the look of a  pirate can be less than desirable  to convincingly create scenes that take  place in the 1700s  it was vital that all the actors who  appeared on screen  looked the part the application of  makeup and prosthetics on an actor can  be a long and grueling process  the complex makeup and costumes worn by  actors can cause extreme discomfort  pain and in some cases physical injuries  which actors experience the most pain  and discomfort due to their makeup  and costumes skarsgard's bootstrap bill  turner had the unique distinction of  being the only member of davy jones crew  who wasn't computer generated however  that may not be as cool as it sounds  skarsgard had to undergo a grueling  makeup process  spending four hours in the chair to  achieve his rotting ship  look and was dubbed bulabase on set  because of the appearance  he said that they couldn't shoot for  more than three days straight because he  would get rashes from the makeup  and when he was done filming for the day  it took an additional hour and a half to  remove the heavy makeup and prosthetics  which wasn't too gentle on the skin we  applaud skarsgard for his commitment to  the role  and even though it sounds painful the  makeup looks great  captain salazar and his crew are some of  the coolest looking beings in the  pirates franchise  and while cgi had a big part in making  that look possible  practical effects were also a major part  in creating the effect  the makeup team went with a cracked  earth look for all the skin on the  cursed pirates  using prosthetics and paints javier  bardem  spent three and a half hours every day  in a chair  getting his makeup and prosthetics done  which became a very repetitive and  tedious process  bardem also had dots and some blue  screen on his face  to help the animators in post the end  result is a truly awesome effect  and all the time that went into making  it was well worth it  well it took me a little while to adjust  to the time frame hector barbosa is one  of the most memorable pirates from the  franchise  and his awesome look is a big part of  that it took about an  hour and a half for jeffrey rush to get  into his full pirate makeup  this included wearing fake rotten teeth  and wearing contact lenses to make his  eyes look more dead  and yellowish having fake teeth and  contact lenses in  all the time wasn't a comfortable  situation even though this caused rush  some discomfort  the end result is a grimy sword-wielding  captain  that is probably the image a lot of  people conjure when thinking of a  back on your pirate cockroaches it's  been  18 years since the curse of the black  pearl was released  so we'll forgive you if you forgot this  character  jacoby was one of barbosa's undead crew  members  who had a very specific physical  attribute his beard was on fire  and this wasn't a camera trick or cgi  the makeup and effects department made a  fake beard with wiring in the dreads  that were used to light incense  which actor vince lozano actually wore  while it was lit  they had to relight his beard between  takes and it's just as dangerous as it  sounds  lizano was burned several times the  beard would occasionally catch on fire  and it would also burn  other people when his beard would flip  into them you kind of always smell  burning hair around this guy  perhaps next time they should use cgi  instead  no fair rigetti is one of the most fun  and lovable characters in the series  with his signature look and fake eye  mackenzie crook  the actor behind righetti didn't  actually have a fake eye  instead he wore multiple different types  of contact lenses while filming  soft lenses were used to give his eyes a  certain grimy look  and hard lenses were used to represent  the fake eye as the lenses physically  bulged out crook's eye  these hard lenses can be very  uncomfortable but righty didn't let that  stop him from putting on  a memorable performance hi  before elizabeth swann became the badass  fighter on the seas  she was the pristine girl who dressed in  perfect clothing  this included a corset in the first  movie which wasn't very comfortable  nightly said that being in a corset is  positively awful  and that it makes it difficult to  breathe  ironically that is the plot point used  when she is in the corset in the movie  luckily for nightly the later movies saw  her wearing more loose-fitting clothing  to adjust for the extra movement and  fighting she was doing  the pirates of the caribbean movies are  extremely large in scale  and this includes a very big cast of  extras  any time you see a pirate on screen a  ton of time  and effort went into creating the look  pirate clothes arrived  new so the crew had to weather and age  them by putting them into a cement mixer  with bricks  they also dirtied the clothes which  meant actors were spending  hours in the hot sun with dirty clothes  on they had upwards of 50 makeup artists  at a time  getting the actors ready and keeping  them looking the right way throughout  the entire shoot  not the most pleasant or comfortable  experience but it definitely sells them  as real pirates  even though the main focus is on the  pirates don't forget the townsfolk that  appear in these films  like the pirate crews there were a ton  of townsfolk extras which required a lot  of clothing  costume designer pennyrose said for the  first film they ordered 900 pieces of  costuming for the extras  and these clothes weren't the most  comfortable to wear  some of the women had to wear tight  corsets just like keira knightley did  and some of the men had to wear tight  necker chiefs  the fittings were done on the fly as  actors were constantly swapping clothes  to get the proper fit  this made things chaotic and difficult  as there were so many extras  that it was nearly impossible to keep  track of it all  rose said the entire process was a mad  house especially since  most of it took place outside in the hot  sun but she definitely achieved the  right look  in the end johnny depp's portrayal of  captain jack sparrow is iconic  and so is his look to create the  signature look we know and love  depp had to go through a very specific  makeup and costuming process  to make sure his look remained  consistent across all  films this included a wig with  dreadlocks  his real beard braided with beads weaved  in his coat  pants boots and of course the iconic hat  what you may not know is that they  actually had multiple pairs of boots for  depth  because depth was getting wet so often  his boots would fill with water  making it difficult and uncomfortable to  walk the solution  was to create boots that could drain the  water more efficiently and the crew was  regularly switching out his boots  between takes  depp also had to wear special contact  lenses during shooting  the sunny days were so bright and  painful that he needed something to  protect his eyes  i had contact lenses made for him that  were actually sunglasses  naomi harris transformed her look to  play tia damma in dead man's chest and  at world's end  she wore a wig black lipstick black  eyeshadow tribal markings and gold and  dirt on her face  along with prosthetic teeth that would  clip in and out  she also filled her mouth with vegetable  dye before each take which meant she had  to say her lines with the dye dripping  out of her mouth  it wasn't the most comfortable  experience but it looked cool and we  appreciate everything she did for the  character  same story different versions and all  are true  to capture the amazing performance of  bill nye and transform him into davy  jones  the crew had an eye in a motion capture  suit for all of his scenes  he can be seen with white dots painted  on his face  along with 